## Flash Cards
// A deck of cards to learn from:  a word on the front, what it means on the back.
// Click the card to turn it over, then say whether you knew it:  the score keeps count,
// and the next card comes up at random.
// What's where, top to bottom:
//   a card:  its two sides, and turning it over
//   the quiz:  the deck, the card showing, the score, and its drawing
//   the deck:  the words to learn
//   start
//   tests


## A card:  a word on the front, what it means on the back
a "flash card" is a view where:
	- its "front" is text
	- its "back" is text
	// which side is up
	- its "side" is one of front or back
	- it "is turned over" if its side is back

	- to turn it over:
		set its side to back if its side is front otherwise front

	// one side at a time:  a click turns it over
	- to draw it:
		return <div part="card" onClick={turn it over}>
			<div part="hint">{"What it means" if its side is back otherwise "Spanish"}</div>
			<div part="word">{its back if it is turned over otherwise its front}</div>
		</div>

// the cards to learn
a "deck" is a list of flash cards


## The quiz:  the deck, the card showing, and the score
quiz is an app where:
	- its "deck" is a new deck
	// the card showing
	- its "card" is a flash card
	// how many you knew, and how many you've tried
	- its "known" is a number
	- its "tried" is a number

	- its "score" is:
		"Nothing tried yet" if its tried is 0
		its known + " of " + its tried + " right" otherwise

	// a card from the deck at random, front up:  never the one just shown
	- to deal a card:
		set others to cards in its deck where it is not the card of quiz
		set its card to a random card in others
		set the side of its card to front

	// you knew it, or you didn't:  counted, then the next card
	- to say i knew it:
		set its known to its known + 1
		set its tried to its tried + 1
		deal a card
	- to say i missed it:
		set its tried to its tried + 1
		deal a card

	- to start over:
		set its known to 0
		set its tried to 0
		deal a card

	// the score, the card, then what you can do:  turn it over, or say how you did
	- to draw it:
		return <div class="Quiz">
			<ui-menu secondary>
				<ui-item type="header">Flash Cards</ui-item>
				<ui-item>{its score}</ui-item>
				<ui-menu position="right">
					<ui-item onClick={start over}>
						<ui-icon name="redo"/>
						Start over
					</ui-item>
				</ui-menu>
			</ui-menu>
			{draw its card}
			<div class="Answers">
				{<ui-button primary onClick={turn its card over}>Show the answer</ui-button> if its card is not turned over otherwise <>
					<ui-button positive icon="check" onClick={say i knew it}>I knew it</ui-button>
					<ui-button negative basic icon="close" onClick={say i missed it}>I missed it</ui-button>
				</>}
			</div>
		</div>


## The deck:  twelve Spanish words -- add your own
to add (word as text) meaning (translation as text):
	add (a new flash card with front = word, back = translation, side = front) to the deck of quiz

add "el gato" meaning "the cat"
add "el perro" meaning "the dog"
add "la casa" meaning "the house"
add "el libro" meaning "the book"
add "la manzana" meaning "the apple"
add "el agua" meaning "the water"
add "la luna" meaning "the moon"
add "el sol" meaning "the sun"
add "la playa" meaning "the beach"
add "el tren" meaning "the train"
add "la llave" meaning "the key"
add "la mariposa" meaning "the butterfly"


## Start
start over
start quiz


## Tests
to test turning a card over
	set the card to a new flash card with front = "el gato", back = "the cat", side = front
	the card is turned over should be no
	turn the card over
	the card is turned over should be yes
	turn the card over
	the side of the card should be front
